<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Novempopulania</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Novempopulana, Aquitania Tertia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Novempopulana was a late Roman province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, formed around 300 from the southern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a>. Its name, 'nine peoples', referred to its Aquitanian tribes, though it later contained twelve civitates. Its capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elusa">Elusa</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eauze">Eauze</a>, and the province formed the basis of the later duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/novempopulania.jpg" alt="Novempopulania" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image has been made by Zorion (User:Zorion) and released under the licenses stated above. You are free to use th... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Novempopulania1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
